<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toamasina</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tamatave</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toamasina, formerly Tamatave, is the main seaport of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, on the island's east coast. In the 18th century it was a trading port of the Betsimisaraka coast, and in 1817 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radama-i">Radama I</a> of the Merina Kingdom took it, bringing the east coast under Merina rule. French forces attacked it in 1845 and 1883, and today it handles most of the country's foreign trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toamasina.jpg" alt="Toamasina" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hanspeter Limacher · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tamatave_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
